1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--topic-writing","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/topic-writing","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/topic-writing","sourceHash":"1be39ef7b0ddb46c8861baf60d759f4ffea15b2f69648496cc47f0d8a4e6e080","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:17.815Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Topic Writing","zh":"主题写作"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Topic Talk is structured writing practice focused on a specific subject, but with multiple attempts. Unlike normal journaling or writing, where you write about whatever comes up, Topic Writing deliberately targets areas where you want to build vocabulary and fluency.","zh":"主题写作是一种围绕特定主题、进行多次尝试的结构化写作练习。它不同于普通的日记或写作——后者通常想到什么就写什么；主题写作会有意识地针对你想积累词汇、提升流利度的领域。"}},{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How It Works","zh":"运作方式"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Choose a topic or piece of media. It can be anything: your job, a news story, a hobby, a hypothetical scenario, an abstract concept. Then set a timer and write about it for 10 minutes, on your own. If you get stuck, look up words!","zh":"选择一个主题或一段媒体内容。可以是任何内容：你的工作、一个新闻故事、一项爱好、一个假设情境或抽象概念。然后设定计时器，独自围绕它写10分钟。如果卡住了，就查词！"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Then, the following day, repeat that exact same topic (without reviewing your old writing). Set another timer for 10 minutes and do the exercise again.","zh":"第二天，重复完全相同的主题（不要回顾之前写的内容）。再次设定10分钟计时器，然后重新进行一次练习。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Do this day after day, using fewer lookups and tools, until you feel confident about the 10 minutes of writing.","zh":"日复一日地练习，逐渐减少查词和工具的使用，直到你对这10分钟的写作感到自信。"}},{"id":"when-its-useful","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When It's Useful","zh":"适用场景"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Topic Writing is especially valuable in:","zh":"主题写作尤其适用于："}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Phase 5A (Writing Comfort):</strong> Giving yourself several attempts at the same topic builds confidence and ease","zh":"<strong>阶段5A（写作适应）：</strong>针对同一主题进行多次尝试，建立信心并逐渐写得更轻松"},{"en":"<strong>Phase 5B (Accuracy):</strong> Writing about complex topics to practice using grammar and vocabulary correctly","zh":"<strong>阶段5B（准确性）：</strong>围绕复杂主题写作，练习正确使用语法和词汇"},{"en":"<strong>Phase 6 (Fluency):</strong> Targeting vocabulary gaps in specific domains and general fluidity","zh":"<strong>阶段6（流利度）：</strong>针对特定领域的词汇空白，提升整体表达流畅度"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"提示"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Prepare a few key words or phrases related to the topic before you start","zh":"开始前准备一些与主题相关的关键词或短语"},{"en":"Don't avoid topics because they're hard — that's where the growth happens","zh":"不要因为主题困难就回避它们——成长正发生在这里"},{"en":"Consider using your writing for <a href=\"/roadmap/library/corrected-reading-aloud\">Corrected Reading Aloud</a>","zh":"考虑将你的写作内容用于<a href=\"/roadmap/library/corrected-reading-aloud\">纠错后朗读</a>"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
